    "Sankara (Hindu Advaita Vedanta philosopher; his understanding of Maya and Brahman cited)",
    "Buddha / Gandhi (mentioned as comparisons to Jesus as masters of Maya)",
    "King-Felix (fictional character from VALIS novel; identified with Christ and the Second Advent)"
  ],
  "texts_works": [
    "VALIS (PKD's novel; referenced as theologically correct exegesis of 2-3-74)",
    "Gospel of Luke (the Acts-Luke diptych; read as account of the real world against Maya)",
    "Acts of the Apostles (treated as Part II of Luke; contains material referenced in Tears)",
    "Q document (possible source of Luke; unclear if PKD means this or the Gospel proper)",
    "Ezekiel 36:27 (prophesy of God filling humans with spirit: 'I will put my spirit into you')",
    "Book of Life (referenced as having PKD's name inscribed)",
    "Frozen Journey (referenced as allegory of autogenerated spurious world)",
    "Hebrew Bible / Old Testament (the Mosaic Law age; contrasted with Gospel grace)",
    "Tears (likely referencing Scripture or PKD's visionary text; treated as cardinal to 2-3-74)"
