  ],
  "tensions": [
    "Uncertainty over whether VALIS is the Holy Spirit or some independent divine intelligence, though PKD argues the identity is invincible",
    "Inconsistency between understanding Jesus as a yogic master of illusory Maya (Hindu framework) and as the Logos/Son of the Judeo-Christian God (theistic framework)",
    "Question of whether Q document or the Gospel of Luke itself is what PKD 'really' means when discussing Acts and Luke as the true account",
    "Unresolved whether the three-age schema (Father/Son/Spirit) maps cleanly onto Joachim del Fiore's schema or introduces a novel theological structure",
    "Tension between determinism (God's plan, the encoding-decoding mechanism) and human freedom ('cosmocrator' with creative imaginative powers)",
    "Incomplete articulation of how 'pure consciousness' as Kantian-style self-awareness of construct-making differs from or relates to Christian mysticism",
    "The claim that Christ 'broke world's power' and thus 'it would only seem to kill him' leaves unresolved whether Christ's resurrection is literal or metaphorical",
    "Assertion of the parousia as imminent or 'already accomplished'—ambiguous temporal reference"
  ],
  "evidence_quotes": [
    "\"What I am saying is that it is all true - including my seeing my name entered in the Book of Life - beginning with 'Tears' & continuing on to my 'dying & being reborn' during Holy Week of this year.\"",
    "\"My internal glimpse of Valis as an encyphering-decyphering 'device' is simply extraordinary. It does not limit itself to the Bible, but Scripture is its codebook (as I've long suspected).\"",
    "\"Pure consciousness makes world but is not compelled to assent to it as his own construct, subject to his creative imaginative powers, his reason: Would this be Valis?\"",
    "\"Jesus came to break the power of the world mechanism over us (known to the Gnostics as heimarmene)... Thus it follows logically that he is still alive (for had he broken world's power, it would only seem to kill him).\"",
    "\"As I realized Tuesday night when, ripped, I read Luke, I was not reading a description of a world, I was in a world + it is the actual world which we suffer the sensory deprivation of in the dream mentioned above.\""
  ],
